  "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $9$th roots of unity?",
  "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $9$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a regular nonagon (regular $9$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/assets/d8a917138beb862f6816fc059847659b1ba11e17d6a7a4906309b021baf1d3e5.png)",
